WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.280
- All right, everybody
let's get to my first guest.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.020
She is not only a beautiful singer,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.700
but also a beautiful person.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.120
We have watched her grow up

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.330
from a Disney Channel star

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.230
to the strong woman she is today.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.770
She's had nine top 20
songs and has been named

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:16.670
one of time's most influential
people, super cool!

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.490
You can see her starting tomorrow,

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.980
flexing her acting skills once again,

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.317
in Eurovision Song Contest,

00:00:22.317 --> 00:00:25.520
"The Story of Fire Saga," on Netflix,

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.450
it's an amazing film, it's awesome.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.860
She's the one and only Demi Lavato.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.620
Hey, what's up Demi, can you hear me?

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.010
- Yeah, I can hear you.
- Oh, good, oh good.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.177
How are you doing?

00:00:35.177 --> 00:00:37.740
- I'm so good, how are you?

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:38.993
- I'm doing all right.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.310
What have you been doing in quarantine?

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.250
Everybody's got a kind of
a different thing going on.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.480
Mine has been filled with kids

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.160
and trying to entertain them like a clown.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.130
What is your life like? (chuckles)

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:51.030
- Mine is taking care of my dogs,

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.160
my fur babies.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.940
So they're my kids and,

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.140
yeah, just spending a
ton of time with them.

00:00:58.541 --> 00:01:03.340
I actually picked up some like
good habits in quarantine,

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.520
which were like--
- Oh!

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.810
- Journaling, I never
used to journal before,

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:09.480
and I picked up journaling,

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:10.560
I picked up yoga,

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.380
which I always hated until now,

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.680
and it's what I needed.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.310
And it was the perfect medicine

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:16.850
for perfect time in my life,

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.360
and, I couldn't be more grateful.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.750
- No, I agree.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:21.950
I've been having the same thing

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.920
and I actually love, I'm
jumping ahead of the interview,

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.590
but it's just kind of a nice segue.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:29.360
I love how open you are
about mental health,

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.300
because I have similar issues

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.980
and I've suffered from depression.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:35.620
I think a lot of people,
especially in the creative world,

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.540
or just from childhood, you've
been kind of trained to like,

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.120
just keep going and you can handle it,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.600
especially as a woman, it's like,

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.050
don't let them see you sweat.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.530
I just love that you're open about that

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.820
because, not everybody's as vulnerable,

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.400
at being like that.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.190
And I think it's helpful for your fans

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:56.380
and 'cause I know in every meet and greet,

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.030
you probably get people
saying that I do too.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:58.863
And they're like,

00:01:58.863 --> 00:02:01.017
"Man, thank you for just
like being open in your songs

00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:02.417
"and open, with everybody,

00:02:02.417 --> 00:02:04.547
"'cause I felt like this was just me

00:02:04.547 --> 00:02:06.067
"and like knowing that somebody else

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.757
"is going through it
makes you not feel alone

00:02:07.757 --> 00:02:09.660
"and so depressed about it."

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.170
So thank you for doing that.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.410
It's really hard.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:13.650
- I just have to say

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:17.740
that, you were like the first idol

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.870
that I ever had and--
- You're so sweet.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:24.040
- I wouldn't be the
artist or even the person

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.370
that I am with being so outspoken

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.880
and vulnerable and fearless

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.510
if I hadn't had you to look up to.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.030
So I thank you for that,

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.660
because--
- Very nice.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.560
- Yes. I just, like,

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.003
I looked at you as my idol growing up,

00:02:40.698 --> 00:02:45.520
you are fearless and
courageous and real as,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.330
and I love that about you

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.530
and I've always just thought to myself,

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:52.390
like when I was younger,

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.223
I always thought to myself,

00:02:53.223 --> 00:02:55.287
"If I ever make it, I wanna be like her,

00:02:55.287 --> 00:02:58.180
"because she's real and she's genuine."

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.160
- And I think the thing about it though,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.037
is even you're saying like,

00:03:02.037 --> 00:03:03.680
"You're strong, you're courageous,
you're all those things,"

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.800
I'm not all the time, it takes work.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.030
Like, that's the thing,

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.608
I think everybody looks at us as like,

00:03:08.608 --> 00:03:11.557
like even when you overcome
something, they're like,

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:12.620
"Okay, well she's already overcome,"

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.530
then I'm like, "No, no,
no, that's a daily effort."

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.220
And like trying to be
positive, that's a daily effort

00:03:18.118 --> 00:03:19.020
and that's not like a given,

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.030
like you're just over it,

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:22.630
you went to some magical
therapy session and it's over.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:26.030
I think that that's a daily
thing that you work at

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:27.420
and a daily thing that I work at,

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.410
and I don't know.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.580
I just thank you for the compliments,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.970
but I just think it's really,

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:31.970
it's a really cool thing

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:34.600
and it's not easy to always
have a spotlight on you

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.380
and arrows being aimed at you,

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.020
especially when you are vulnerable

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:39.700
and you give people more ammo

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:41.590
for all the stories out there.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.170
So anyway, but thank you for doing that.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.450
I love, and I don't even know
if you saw me tweet about,

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.680
I was jamming so hard to your new single.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.613
I love it.
- Aw, thank you Kelly so much.

00:03:51.613 --> 00:03:52.446
- I love it!

00:03:52.446 --> 00:03:53.640
I think it's such a,

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.800
it's like refreshing
whenever you hear a song too,

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.920
and you haven't heard it saying like that,

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.680
you haven't heard the message
kind of twisted like that.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:00.630
And I was like, "Whoa!"

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.667
I was like, "That was a
really powerful message,

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:03.780
"but cleverly done."

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.490
And I'm telling you what,

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:08.672
Jedi Level Sabotage, (both chuckle)

00:04:08.672 --> 00:04:11.833
is legit, my favorite lyric
I've heard in a very long time,

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.730
what inspired this song?

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.870
Is it just your life

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:19.463
and kind of just really daily
kind of figuring out you?

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.550
- Yes.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:24.530
I actually wrote that song last summer

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.453
and recorded it last summer.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.810
And I did it with my producer Oak Felder,

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:34.990
who I did "Sorry Not Sorry"
with and a bunch of other songs.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.450
- I love him, he's great!

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.060
- Yes, he's so great.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.170
You know he's obsessed with Star Wars.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.710
So he had this Star Wars
memorabilia in his studio,

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.877
and he came up with that
lyric and I was like,

00:04:44.877 --> 00:04:45.710
"Oh, that's genius.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.820
"We gotta put that in there."

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.210
But yeah, I just like the message,

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:54.420
I felt like I wasn't
being authentic to people

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:57.890
because I've been editing pictures.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:00.760
Like, I had gone on a vacation
to Bora Bora last year

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.460
and I edited the bikini
pictures and I posted them

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:05.310
and I got a bunch of likes,

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:06.410
but it didn't feel good

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.800
because I was putting up
something that wasn't real.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.532
I felt like I was catfishing everybody.

00:05:12.532 --> 00:05:13.830
- But at some point you probably felt

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.090
the need to do that because
everybody does that.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.990
And like, if you do come out looking real,

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:19.540
it's like, people don't even know

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.060
what that's supposed to look like anymore.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.520
- Yes, it's like teenagers.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.690
I wouldn't be surprised if
they didn't know what cellulite

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:28.450
or stretch marks look like

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.490
until they pop up on their body,

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:31.360
and then all of a sudden they have

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.950
to face students out of their pictures

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.620
because I'm doing it,

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:35.710
and they see me doing.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.597
So I was like, "No, I need to change this.

00:05:37.597 --> 00:05:38.777
"I need to change the narrative,

00:05:38.777 --> 00:05:41.730
"I need to like post something real."

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.240
And so I posted something

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.610
while I was like in the studio

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.390
and it was that unedited bikini picture.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:48.720
And it just felt so good

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:51.810
because I had a few crushes at the time,

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.770
and it was interesting to see
that all of those crushes,

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.330
they actually liked that picture

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.070
where all of cellulite was out

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:00.477
and I wasn't touched up and I was like,

00:06:00.477 --> 00:06:01.310
"Oh my gosh!"

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.490
Like, here's these people
I was trying to impress,

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:04.760
they were the ones I
was trying to impress,

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.100
not people like fans or anything,

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.740
I know that they accept
me and love me for me,

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:12.250
but, I was trying to
look hot for my crushes.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:13.083
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:13.083 --> 00:06:14.650
- And then they--
- At some point it's like,

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.970
well, they're gonna see ya',

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.430
eventually.
- Exactly

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.736
and I don't want them to like,
think I'm catfishing them.

00:06:20.736 --> 00:06:22.400
- Yeah.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.320
- Anyways, I felt that
was like the first step

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:29.350
in kind of owning, taking the power back

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:32.060
from what other people were placing,

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:34.260
the judgments people
were placing on my body,

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.967
I got to take the power back and be like,

00:06:35.967 --> 00:06:37.657
"Okay, you really wanna judge me here?

00:06:37.657 --> 00:06:39.040
"Here it is."

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:39.873
- Yeah.

00:06:39.873 --> 00:06:41.980
- Nothing that you say is going to affect

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.460
what the strength and the love

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.130
that I have for myself up here.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.540
So come out clean.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.160
- I feel like it's really freeing

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.260
'cause we're both women in an industry

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.190
that is hard on women and harder on women.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:56.510
All right, so Demi,
you've been very vocal,

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:59.910
which I appreciate because
we have gigantic platforms

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.700
that I think we should use.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:04.040
But you've been pretty vocal
about "Black Lives Matter."

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:07.464
So, what do you think personally,

00:07:07.464 --> 00:07:10.290
that we can all do differently?

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.930
- I think the first step
is educating ourselves.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.850
We have a lot of time
on our hands right now.

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:16.970
There is no reason why

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.540
we shouldn't be watching these movies,

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.260
watching and absorbing in all information

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:24.870
that we possibly can about
what's going on in the world.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:27.870
And then, from there,

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:32.314
we've seen it all over the
media, that being silent

00:07:32.314 --> 00:07:35.630
and being not racist
is not enough anymore.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:38.840
And, that's kind of
something that I posted,

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:42.290
posted about, like a month ago

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.780
when the Arbery robbery stuff happened,

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:45.723
I was like,

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.620
I saw online what had happened

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.460
and I felt this overwhelming sense of like

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:56.020
frustration, anger, I was like crying

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.203
and I started writing in my phone.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.340
I just got to all my emotions

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.560
and I felt guilty that
I hadn't been doing more

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:08.810
and saying more, as an ally.

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:11.133
But I was also afraid,

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:15.823
that people were going to come at me.

00:08:16.978 --> 00:08:17.980
- Cause they will.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:21.490
- Yes, because everybody's
angry right now,

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:23.270
and I just didn't want anyone to think

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:26.780
that I had the wrong intentions
or that I was uneducated.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:30.070
Like, speaking about something
that I didn't know about,

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.550
that was a fear of mine.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:35.243
And so I kind of, when that happened,

00:08:36.423 --> 00:08:39.850
and even before I found
out about George Floyd,

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.697
I was like, "No, I need to do more,

00:08:41.697 --> 00:08:42.867
"I need to be an ally,

00:08:42.867 --> 00:08:43.970
"I have not been an ally."

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:47.300
I have like Aretha Franklin,

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.140
Billie Holiday, Whitney Houston

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:53.180
these women of color have
like shaped my musical journey

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:58.180
and how am I supposed
appreciate what they've given me

00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:01.460
and not stand out for their community.

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:05.430
And so I just, I switched my thinking

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.523
and then all of this happened and,

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.820
I wish I had kind of come
to that realization sooner,

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:14.350
but I think everything
happens in its own timing,

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.270
and I've now gotten to a place where like,

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:19.610
because I'm able to deal with
my own demons, my own things,

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:23.610
I can now kind of help,
advocate for other people.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.170
And I think maybe that's a reason why

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:26.820
some people aren't speaking out

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.120
and doing things is they're afraid,

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.770
but they're also like not
ready to help other people.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:35.050
I dunno, I just wanted to be the ally

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.630
that I know I can be,

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.640
and, I want to be able
to shift the thinking

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.490
as much as possible because,

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:43.370
the legacy that I will leave as a person

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.130
will last so much longer than the music

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:46.570
that we leave behind.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:47.480
- Yeah, totally.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:48.910
Your character means everything.

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:49.753
I agree.

